  "body": "## what\n\n- `main.tf`: pass `manual_snapshot_retention_period` through to `aws_redshift_cluster`\n- `variables.tf`: add the variable with `default = -1`, the provider default\n\n## why\n\n`aws_redshift_cluster` accepts `manual_snapshot_retention_period`, but the module never sets it, so the attribute cannot be managed through the module at all.\n\nThat matters most when adopting an existing cluster. If the cluster's value differs from the provider default, it surfaces as drift on every plan and the caller has no variable to resolve it with.\n\nThe default of `-1` is the provider's own, meaning snapshots are retained indefinitely, so nothing changes for existing callers.\n\n## notes\n\nStacked behind cloudposse/terraform-aws-redshift-cluster#51, which touches the same two files. Happy to rebase once that lands, or to fold the two together if you would rather review one PR.\n",
  "created_at": "2026-09-11T14:45:06Z",
